# Architecture

Purpose:
  System architecture knowledge base. Defines architecture levels,
  patterns, principles, scaling, availability, data, observability,
  networking, and deployment rules.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1 @INDEX.sdd
   2 @architecture.sdd (architecture overview)
   3 @levels.sdd (ProjectScale L0-L5)
   4 @patterns.sdd (architecture patterns)
   5 @principles.sdd (architecture principles)
   6 @scaling.sdd (scaling rules)
   7 @availability.sdd (availability/RTO/RPO)
   8 @data.sdd (data architecture)
   9 @observability.sdd (observability)
   10 @networking.sdd (networking)
   11 @deployment.sdd (deployment)

Rules:
  [AR1] Architecture MUST be defined before implementation.
  [AR2] Architecture patterns MUST be documented.
  [AR3] Scaling rules MUST be defined for L3+ systems.
  [AR4] Availability targets MUST be explicit.
  [AR5] Data architecture MUST include storage, flow, and retention.

Navigation:
  Architecture: @architecture.sdd
  Levels: @levels.sdd
  Patterns: @patterns.sdd
  Principles: @principles.sdd
  Scaling: @scaling.sdd
  Availability: @availability.sdd
  Data: @data.sdd
  Observability: @observability.sdd
  Networking: @networking.sdd
  Deployment: @deployment.sdd
  ProjectArchitecture: @../instances/vkard.az/architecture/INDEX.sdd

State: +
